# EvalRouter

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) at the repo root before you change code. That file is the project guideline for coding agents.

`EVALROUTER_REQUIREMENTS.md` is v0 product truth. It is frozen unless the user explicitly asks to change the spec. Do not edit `spec/`.

`EVALROUTER_RUNTIME_REQUIREMENTS.md` is Live product truth. Frozen unless the user explicitly asks. `RUNTIME_BUILD.md` is the Live build order. Do not auto-start Live slices; v0 is done.

`BUILD.md` is the v0 build order. Do not put build order inside a spec.

Product jobs (J1–J8) are BDD. A slice is done when Given / When / Then holds.

Implementation (API, runner, MCP) uses TDD. Write a failing unit or integration test, then code. CI failing the build on a named-model eval miss is J7, not TDD.

Evals are product checks, not unit tests. Do not call evals "tests" in product copy.

Write spec text, product copy, and user-facing strings in ASD-STE100. See AGENTS.md “Language”.

After a slice review passes, write `build/handoffs/slice-N.md` and start slice N+1 at once. Do not wait for the user. See AGENTS.md “Slice loop”.
